WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:02.388
Unit 3 is the parallel run.

2
00:00:02.388 --> 00:00:06.732
The order is create, validate,
disable, observe for thirty days,

3
00:00:06.732 --> 00:00:09.749
then drop, and it's
required for production.

4
00:00:09.749 --> 00:00:13.362
While both logins work, there
are three exit criteria.

5
00:00:13.362 --> 00:00:17.001
Every application and job also
appears on its Entra login.

6
00:00:17.001 --> 00:00:19.388
No remote N T L M remains.

7
00:00:19.388 --> 00:00:22.312
And nothing still arrives
only on the legacy login.

8
00:00:22.312 --> 00:00:27.437
Connections made on the server itself
always report N T L M, so they don't count.

9
00:00:27.437 --> 00:00:29.538
A snapshot is only a moment.

10
00:00:29.538 --> 00:00:33.476
Sequel Server Audit's successful
login group records the whole window.

11
00:00:33.476 --> 00:00:38.537
The cutover disables a Windows user or a
sequel login, and the rollback enables it.

12
00:00:38.537 --> 00:00:41.002
A Windows group can't
be disabled that way,

13
00:00:41.002 --> 00:00:44.988
so the kit denies it connect sequel,
and the rollback grants it back.

14
00:00:44.988 --> 00:00:46.324
Nothing is dropped.

15
00:00:46.324 --> 00:00:50.125
The S A account is disabled
and renamed, never migrated.

16
00:00:50.125 --> 00:00:53.500
And the kit's judge reports
readiness for each legacy login.

17
00:00:53.500 --> 00:00:55.300
It never disables anything.
